We first rewrite the map in a more compact form in terms of the Frobenius norm of $( m{y}_{\mathcal{D}} -  m{z})$: $ orall\,\,\,\,  m{z} \in \mathbb{R}^{n_L 	imes k}$,  egin{equation*} \mathcal{L}( m{z};  m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}) =  rac{1}{\left(2 \pi \sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2ight)^{n_L k / 2}} \exp{- rac{1}{2\sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2} 
