orm{ m{y}_{\mathcal{D}} -  m{z}}_F^2}ight) 2 ( m{y}_{\mathcal{D}} -  m{z}) \left(-  m{I}_{n_L 	imes k}ight) =  rac{ m{y}_{\mathcal{D}} -  m{z}}{\sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2} \mathcal{L}( m{z};  m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}). \end{aligned} \end{equation*} To find the supremum of $h: \mathbb{R}^{n_L 	imes k} 	o \mathbb{R}$,  egin{equation*} h( m{z}) \coloneqq 
orm{ rac{\partial}{\partial  m{z}} \mathcal{L}( m{z};  m{y}_{\mathcal{D}})}_F =  rac{
