orm{ m{y}_{\mathcal{D}} -  m{z}}_F^2 / \sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2 = 1$. \ For any such $ m{z}_0$ we would have that  egin{equation*} h( m{z}_0) = \mathcal{L}\left( m{z}_0;  m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}ight) =  rac{1}{\sqrt{\sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2}}  rac{e^{-1/2}}{\left(2 \pi \sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2ight)^{n_L k / 2}}. \end{equation*} It is also possible to define  egin{equation*} l: \mathbb{R}^+ 	o \mathbb{R}, \ l(x) \coloneqq  rac{x}{\sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2}  rac{1}{\left(2 \pi \sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2ight)^{n_L k / 2}} \exp{- rac{1}{2 \sigma_{\scalebox{0.65}{$\kern-3pt m{y}_{\mathcal{D}}$}}^2} x^2}, \  orall\,\,\,\, x \in \mathbb{R}^+, \end{equation*} which, by construction, has the following property:  egin{equation*}  orall\,\,\,\,  m{z} \in \mathbb{R}^{n_L 	imes k}, \ l(
