orm{ m{v}}_F^2)$ (see \cref{eq:ineqnormsqleq}) and performing the change of variable $ m{u} \coloneqq  m{v} / (\sigma^2)^{1/2}$. The conclusion for the lower bound follows easily observing that $ m{K}'( m{x})$ is positive definite, so it holds  egin{equation*} ( m{K}'( m{x})^{-1} + 2 \cdot  m{I}_k) \otimes_K  m{I}_{n_L} \in \operatorname{Sym}_+^{n_L k}, \end{equation*} and therefore given $ m{u}_{\mathrm{f}} =  latten{ m{u}}$ the integral in \cref{eq:nngpexplikgeq} is equal to a constant depending on $ m{x},  m{\varphi}, \left( m{\sigma}_light)_{l = 1}^{L - 1}, n_L$:  egin{equation}  egin{aligned} & \int_{\mathbb{R}^{n_L 	imes k}} \exp{- rac{1}{2} ( m{u}_{\mathrm{f}}^T \left(( m{K}'( m{x})^{-1} + 2 \cdot  m{I}_k) \otimes_K  m{I}_{n_L}ight)  m{u}_{\mathrm{f}})} d m{u}_{\mathrm{f}} = \ & \kern20pt = \left((2\pi)^{k} \det{ m{K}'( m{x})^{-1} + 2 \cdot  m{I}_k}ight)^{n_L / 2}. \end{aligned} \end{equation} 	extbf{Upper bound.} For the upper bound the procedure is similar. Starting from the result in \cref{eq:nngpexplikprop}, applying the inequality $
